From f025eca510c51ad21de695f73ea82fbbecd26c05 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nabils <nabileo477@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 06:54:34 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] Set kernel size in deconvolution args when loading a PSF

load_kernel updated com.kernelsize but left args->ks unchanged, so
anything keyed on args->ks (for example the choice between the naive
and FFT Richardson-Lucy paths and the memory estimate) used a stale
size after a PSF was loaded from file. Copy the loaded size to args->ks.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/filters/deconvolution.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/filters/deconvolution.c b/src/filters/deconvolution.c
index 51c8c4c..03499a8 100644
--- a/src/filters/deconvolution.c
+++ b/src/filters/deconvolution.c
@@ -245,6 +245,7 @@ int load_kernel(gchar* filename, estk_data *args) {
 		orig_size = com.kernelsize;
 	}
 	com.kernelchannels = load_fit.naxes[2];
+	args->ks = com.kernelsize;
 	args->kchans = com.kernelchannels;
 	gui_function(set_kernel_size_in_gui, NULL);
 
-- 
